<title>USA: John Simplot cuts Boise Cascade stake.</title>
<headline>John Simplot cuts Boise Cascade stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Simplot, the Idaho potato magnate, said Tuesday he reduced his stake in Boise Cascade Corp to 4.923 percent, from 6.12 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, Simplot said he sold 577,800 shares of Boise Cascade between October 18 and 31 at prices ranging from $30.531 to $31.750 a share.</p>
</text>
